{
  "title": "Differential pair",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "SKY130 NFET differential pair: tanh transfer, sweep V(in+) with the tail current stepped 0.1/0.2/0.4 mA",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 60,
        "y": -193,
        "title": "Differential pair — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A SKY130 nfet_01v8 differential pair: MN1 and MN2",
          "(W = 10 um, L = 0.15 um) share a tail current IT and",
          "load resistors RD1 = RD2 = 4 kohm to VDD = 1.8 V. VCM",
          "holds MN2's gate at 0.9 V while the sweep ramps VIN",
          "(MN1's gate) from 0.5 to 1.3 V. The pair steers IT",
          "between the two sides as a tanh of the input difference,",
          "so probes voutp and voutn split apart and cross at",
          "VIN = VCM. Both bulks are grounded (GBK1, GBK2). IT is",
          "stepped 0.1/0.2/0.4 mA to show steeper transfer at more",
          "tail.",
          "",
          "Set VCM.V = 0.8 and re-run to move the crossover point."
        ]
      }
    ],
